  "note": "Total Assets = Total Liabilities + Equity reconciles exactly. DISCREPANCY FOUND (source-document-internal, not an extraction error): this report's own discrete Jul-Sep'11 column is self-consistent throughout (net interest income through PBT through net profit all reconcile via a-b-d-tax exactly), but that self-consistent chain starts from a 'Net interest income' of 642,035,749 that is 821,247 BDT (0.13%) higher than interest income (3,329,998,737) minus interest paid (2,687,141,741) = 642,856,996 would imply. This small internal wrinkle compounds: Q1'11 (358,679,869) + Q2'11 (114,380,106) + this file's discrete Q3'11 (226,200,945) = 699,260,920, which is 924,494 BDT (0.13%) below the report's own printed Jan-Sep'11 cumulative of 700,185,414. Both the discrete-quarter figures (fully self-consistent as their own column) and the cumulative figure are recorded here as reported, per project convention of recording rather than silently reconciling a divergence; the gap is small (~0.13%) and specific to this one unaudited quarterly filing."
